^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Multi-argument std::function construction.  Layer-1 partial-spec pack deduction
(cpp11_partial_spec_pack_after_fixed) is fixed, so the converting constructor
now resolves; previously this passed only VACUOUSLY ("found no match for symbol
'function'").  The remaining gap: the handler pointers _M_invoker / _M_manager
are not assigned during multi-argument construction, so operator() dereferences
a null _M_invoker.  Single-argument std::function invokes correctly and soundly
(N5008 [func.wrap.func]), so this is specific to the _Function_handler<R(A...),
F> pack shape.  Flip to CORE once the multi-argument handler wiring is fixed.
